  <reporting-org ref="47045" secondary-reporter="0" type="30">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Global Fund to Fight AIDS, Tuberculosis and Malaria</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Increasing Access and promoting comprehensive Care,Support and Treatment - India (01-Oct-2015-31-Dec-2017)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">India, HIV, Department of Economic Affairs, Ministry of Finance of India (DEA-H)This program has the following goals: Provide comprehensive care and support to all persons living with HIV/AIDS and treatment services for all those who require it..  Reduce new infections by 50% (2007 Baseline of NACP III). The objectives of this program are: Early linkages of PLHIV including key population to Care ,Support and treatment services and retention in care continuum.  To improve coverage of PMTCT services through enhanced access in public and private sector and working towards ellimination of paediatric HIV and keeping mothers alive healthy.  To provide Universal Access to ART for all PLHIV including key population to reduce morbidity and moratlity related to HIV &amp; HIV-TB coinfection and also to reduce transmission risks.  To strenghen evidence for guiding future policy for HIV and TB care and prevention.  To strengthen community system for both HIV and TB care and reduction in stigma and discrimination.  To strengthen systems for prevention, early diagnosis and treatment of TB and HIV in co-infected individuals for improved outcomes.  To strengthen systems to enhance access to both TB and HIV services, quality of care, monitoring &amp; evaluation</narrative>
  </description>
